# tools/compose_tiled_witness.rish -- a source pattern TILED to fill a box proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the CSS background-repeat sibling of tools/compose_witness.rish: where compose
# lays ONE picture over a target at a point, this rung lays MANY, tiling a small source pattern across a rectangle edge
# to edge (a texture, a wallpaper, a small motif that fills a panel). Stands on the open compositing verb
# (image/compose.rye paint_over_region) and the open QOI codec (image/qoi.rye), adding no new pixel loop.
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS spec -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that a small pattern becomes a filled box: paint_tiled paves the rectangle with copies
# of the pattern, tiled from the corner, a boundary tile the pattern size does not divide CLIPPED to the box edge (its
# top-left window). An evenly-dividing pattern paves an exact grid of copies (each pixel its pattern color by the pure
# modulo); a non-dividing box clips the last band and still paves the whole box with no gap; a translucent pattern
# blends src-over uniform; the tiled image round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; a sub-rectangle paves
# only its own box; a pattern larger than the box is itself clipped; a zero dimension, an empty pattern, and an
# out-of-bounds box each refuse by name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- compose owns the blit, qoi owns
# the buffers; this rung only routes each tile to its window and its clip. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/compose_tiled_witness.rish

say "compose-tiled: Language EN -- Season G's background-repeat verb; a keeper names a pattern and a box and reads back the box paved with copies of the pattern, on our own open geometry and codec."
say "compose-tiled: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; image/compose.rye paint_over_region OWNS the blit, image/qoi.rye owns both buffers, and this rung only ROUTES each tile to its window and its clip so a translucent pattern tiles over the ground beneath it."
say "compose-tiled: Lens TAME -- the whole box bound-checked ONCE up front in u64 so a far edge can never wrap; the tile count a ceiling division so a boundary tile is clipped not dropped; the tile partition in u32 so it never wraps; all-or-nothing so a refusal paints nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/compose_tiled"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/compose_tiled.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "compose-tiled: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "compose-tiled: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "compose-tiled: ${out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "printf '%s' '${out}' | grep -q 'GREEN image-compose-tiled' && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "compose-tiled: selftest did not print the GREEN compose-tiled line"

say "compose-tiled: GREEN -- a source pattern tiled to fill a box, proven on metal: an exact grid of copies, a clipped boundary tile, a translucent src-over tile, a byte-for-byte QOI round trip, and every malformed fill refused by name having painted nothing."
